# same_bare_method_dispatch.tkr — a NAMESPACE-IDENTITY project-regressor (0.3.1
# regressor-principal, §5 triage exception): three classes sharing the SAME bare name `Svc`
# across three namespaces (`left`/`right`/a `aaa_decoy` sorted-first poison decoy) — an
# INSTANCE method call must dispatch to the canonically-namespaced class, never a
# readdir-order same-bare collision (issue #290). Flattening into one snippet would collide
# all three `Svc` types outright. Kept on disk, unflattened; not inline-scenario-izable.

#
# UNFOLD (2026-07-26, owner ruling "está proibido inline code em tkr"): this project is also a HOST
# for scenarios that used to be `Given source inline` blocks in regressor.tkr. Each is a MEMBER
# NAMESPACE under `src/`, selected by `TEKO_REGR_ENTRY`, and every one of them runs off THIS
# project's SINGLE build — the runner compiles a project's `.tkp` at most once per `.tkr`
# (`RegrBuilt`), and the members differ only by the env selector, args and stdin, never by source.
# The project's own scenario is unchanged and still runs from the same binary with no selector set.

Feature: same_bare_method_dispatch — same-bare-name class instance methods dispatch by canonical namespace

  Scenario: left::Svc and right::Svc, sharing the bare name Svc, each dispatch tag_of to their own instance
    When built and run
    Then exit = 10

