Feature: F9 romaneio .31 — the audit's positive regressions (backend x scenario) (unfolded from regressor.tkr — members of this project's single build)

  # (B-S1) The own backend coerces into a null-union at EVERY placement that declares a type, not
  # only at the binding: `x = null` after a `T | null` binding used to write a raw `const 0` into the
  # VReg the `match` then reads as the wrapper's base address — a load from address 0. The `c` rows
  # are the differential control: the C backend wrapped at the assign all along.

  Scenario: d1_boundary_widen_cast_compiles
    Given env = ["TEKO_REGR_ENTRY=q185_d1_boundary_widen_cast_compiles"]
    When built and run
    Then exit = 42

  # (A-S3) PARITY between the arithmetic and the comparison site of the same D1 decision: a pair of
  # casts guards against flagging in BOTH, so these two spellings of the same operands must agree.
  # Before the shared predicate, `(a to i64) - (b to i64)` compiled and `(a to i64) < (b to i64)` was
  # a hard error — the comparison site called the predicate raw, without the arithmetic site's guards.

